# World 2's wind gusts and the windsock (SPEC 11, "World 2, slice 2", slice B). Ctrl+L, W, 5 starts mission 5 at the base pad; skill 4 is
# pinned after the world has loaded (gusts are on from skill 2; 4-5 also near barracks), ghost on (nothing hurts the chopper).
# The chopper hovers in the strait between the second and fourth island (no jet there, radar zones: tests/w2radar.agk), beside the
# second island's windsock (x 2280): the first gust's tell is not before 18 s of play, the sock whips (limp and full), the push
# comes 50 frames after the tell and moves the chopper sideways, toward +x, by about 37 px, and the sock stays full while it blows.
# No sound is made (no sample is drawn for the plan's howl): the sock is the warning. The unit tests (testW2Gust*) hold the rules.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x05
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 400
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x04
wait 30
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x24
wait 30
press fire 2
wait 60
press up 60
press left 560
wait-serial "mission=1 x=24" 200
screenshot calm
wait-serial "AGK gust tell" 1500
screenshot tell1
wait 2
screenshot tell2
wait 4
screenshot tell3
wait-serial "AGK gust start" 100
wait 3
screenshot push
wait 150
screenshot after
wait 70
# the sock is red (0xD42) in the full frame, which it holds while the gust blows (its whipping: testW2SockIsDrawnAndWhips)
expect-color push 74 225 0xD42 near 3
# the push: toward +x by about 37 px (2420 -> 2457)
expect-serial "mission=1 x=245[5-9] "
expect-serial "AGK gust tell[\s\S]*AGK gust start"
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-min-chip-free 96
